The contract implements a payment splitting mechanism but contains a critical flaw in account closure validation.
### Vulnerability: Unchecked Close Remainder To
### Explanation: The contract fails to validate the `close_remainder_to` field in the account closure branch (when group size ≠ 2), allowing an attacker to specify an arbitrary address that will receive the remaining account balance when the close function is called.
### Risk: Critical - Complete loss of account funds to an attacker-controlled address
